"3 Weeks Later"

186
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,770
Oh, Fuen. What are you up to, honey?

187
00:19:22,230 --> 00:19:23,470
Washing the car, Mom.

188
00:19:23,470 --> 00:19:24,570
What does it look like?

189
00:19:24,570 --> 00:19:28,830
Physics usually comes over to wash it for you. Where is he today?

190
00:19:30,330 --> 00:19:32,670
Why would I ask him? I can do it myself.

191
00:19:32,670 --> 00:19:34,430
Is something going on?

192
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:38,200
If you don't stop asking, I'm washing you too.

193
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:41,900
Fine, suit yourself. Look how clumsy you are. Whatever you say.

194
00:20:59,030 --> 00:21:05,330
"You really don't want to see me anymore, Fuen?"

195
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,870
"Fuen, I'm sorry. I miss you."

196
00:22:36,100 --> 00:22:40,930
"Done with tutoring."

197
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:49,800
If we talk in here, it's not cheating, right?

198
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:52,870
Because we're talking through pictures.

199
00:23:09,670 --> 00:23:14,730
"Done with tutoring."

200
00:23:58,170 --> 00:24:01,900
Oh, Din. How long have you been here?

201
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:04,930
Why didn't you have someone let you in?

202
00:24:04,930 --> 00:24:07,870
Or is something up?

203
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:12,530
Well, I wanted to ask you to go to school with me.

204
00:24:15,330 --> 00:24:16,400
Perfect timing.

205
00:24:16,670 --> 00:24:18,470
I'm in a rush to get to a meeting.

206
00:24:19,130 --> 00:24:21,400
Star, you go with Din, then.

207
00:24:21,730 --> 00:24:22,930
Okay.

208
00:24:24,400 --> 00:24:27,600
Go on, get out. You'll be late for school.

209
00:24:27,600 --> 00:24:29,500
Yes, Dad.

210
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:36,300
Hey, it's the second term. Study hard, you two.

211
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,900
Samai, let's go.

212
00:24:38,900 --> 00:24:40,630
Let the kids do their flirting.

213
00:24:41,330 --> 00:24:42,700
Goodbye.

214
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:51,900
So, we...

215
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:17,130
Come with me.

216
00:25:52,300 --> 00:25:54,070
First time?

217
00:25:55,770 --> 00:25:57,070
Yeah.

218
00:25:57,070 --> 00:25:59,670
Ride the BTS with me more and you'll get the hang of it.

219
00:26:00,700 --> 00:26:03,500
So you're going to take me every day?

220
00:26:03,500 --> 00:26:07,230
If you don't mind the hassle, I'd like to.

221
00:26:07,230 --> 00:26:10,670
Then next time you come, wait inside the house.

222
00:26:10,670 --> 00:26:12,600
Don't stand out in the sun.

223
00:27:05,900 --> 00:27:06,900
Honey.

224
00:27:07,300 --> 00:27:09,570
You still haven't made up with Physics?

225
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:14,670
How do you know?

226
00:27:15,930 --> 00:27:21,570
I'm your mother. Come on, tell me.

227
00:27:28,070 --> 00:27:30,100
Physics is going to study abroad.

228
00:27:30,700 --> 00:27:32,800
But he never told me.

229
00:27:32,800 --> 00:27:36,300
And then he has the nerve to say it all depends on my answer.

230
00:27:36,530 --> 00:27:38,130
Think about it, Mom.

231
00:27:38,130 --> 00:27:40,370
Say I don't agree to be his boyfriend.

232
00:27:40,370 --> 00:27:42,070
Then he'll just leave me.

233
00:27:42,770 --> 00:27:45,470
How am I supposed to not be hurt?

234
00:27:45,470 --> 00:27:46,970
I'm hurt.

235
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:54,400
Honey, are you sure you're not imagining things?

236
00:27:55,930 --> 00:27:59,400
Did Physics actually say that if you won't be his boyfriend,

237
00:27:59,400 --> 00:28:01,500
he'll leave you?

238
00:28:02,470 --> 00:28:03,500
Well...

239
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:09,530
See? You're imagining it.

240
00:28:11,830 --> 00:28:14,530
The university over there already accepted him.

241
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:18,330
Whatever I answer, he's going anyway.

242
00:28:18,330 --> 00:28:21,230
So are you mad that Physics didn't tell you,

243
00:28:21,230 --> 00:28:23,470
or that you'll be apart?

244
00:28:28,230 --> 00:28:32,470
I want to be with him. Wherever we study,

245
00:28:33,200 --> 00:28:37,230
whatever faculty, I wouldn't mind.

246
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:41,030
I just never thought we'd suddenly be so far apart.

247
00:28:41,900 --> 00:28:44,500
But have you thought about it from Physics's side?

248
00:28:44,500 --> 00:28:47,900
About why he wants an answer from you?

249
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:55,770
That's not right, Mom. This is his future.

250
00:28:56,430 --> 00:28:59,200
What if he doesn't want to go because of me?

251
00:29:01,270 --> 00:29:03,400
I don't want to hold him back.

252
00:29:08,570 --> 00:29:11,800
Thanks for breakfast today, Mom.

253
00:29:11,800 --> 00:29:14,030
But you stay here at the shop today.

254
00:29:14,030 --> 00:29:16,370
I'll take the BTS myself.

255
00:29:17,300 --> 00:29:18,400
Bye, Mom.

256
00:29:27,070 --> 00:29:32,800
This second term, I want all Thapfah students to work hard and stay disciplined.

257
00:29:32,800 --> 00:29:36,730
You all did very well last term.

258
00:30:07,730 --> 00:30:10,270
Physics, let's talk.

259
00:30:21,800 --> 00:30:23,430
I'm sorry.

260
00:30:28,600 --> 00:30:30,930
I know I shouldn't have lost my temper.

261
00:30:32,830 --> 00:30:35,170
At the very least, I should've heard you out.

262
00:30:38,100 --> 00:30:40,430
Because you always have your reasons.

263
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:50,200
I get that you're mad at me.

264
00:30:54,030 --> 00:30:57,300
But when you said you didn't want to see my face,

265
00:31:01,100 --> 00:31:03,200
I was lost.

266
00:31:06,430 --> 00:31:11,330
I'm sorry, but I want you to think about your future.

267
00:31:21,400 --> 00:31:23,270
You should go, Physics.

268
00:31:32,530 --> 00:31:34,300
Then can you tell me

269
00:31:35,170 --> 00:31:37,500
how you feel about me?

270
00:31:50,400 --> 00:31:51,530
It hurts

271
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:59,300
that I can't even imagine who I'd be without you.

272
00:32:03,800 --> 00:32:09,300
Even in university, I want to be at the same school as you.

273
00:32:13,200 --> 00:32:15,530
Even though that's not possible anymore,

274
00:32:16,830 --> 00:32:18,430
I'll hang in there.

275
00:32:23,670 --> 00:32:25,100
So...

276
00:32:28,100 --> 00:32:30,300
Summer break, long holidays...

277
00:32:31,900 --> 00:32:36,770
come back to me. Because...

278
00:32:41,170 --> 00:32:44,030
I like you, Physics.

279
00:33:15,230 --> 00:33:18,200
Who said I'm going alone?

280
00:33:19,100 --> 00:33:20,700
Huh?

281
00:33:24,800 --> 00:33:26,330
You...

282
00:33:28,570 --> 00:33:30,470
Come study in England with me.

283
00:33:31,900 --> 00:33:33,600
How is that even possible?

284
00:33:33,600 --> 00:33:35,600
Have you seen my grades?

285
00:33:36,200 --> 00:33:37,470
That's fine.

286
00:33:37,470 --> 00:33:38,870
I'll help you.

287
00:33:39,670 --> 00:33:41,270
Just come with me.

288
00:33:43,270 --> 00:33:45,530
Didn't you already take the exams?

289
00:33:46,030 --> 00:33:50,270
A-Level and IELTS still have a second round.

290
00:33:51,130 --> 00:33:53,330
Pass this round, and you'll still make it in time.

291
00:33:56,130 --> 00:33:58,170
You've got it all planned out, huh?

292
00:34:04,370 --> 00:34:08,800
Well, every plan in my life...

293
00:34:10,370 --> 00:34:12,800
has always had you in it.

294
00:34:36,330 --> 00:34:37,600
It's identical.

295
00:34:37,600 --> 00:34:39,300
Identical how?

296
00:35:37,230 --> 00:35:38,500
Want breakfast?

297
00:35:46,500 --> 00:35:47,770
What?

298
00:35:56,970 --> 00:35:58,670
What's up?

299
00:36:08,630 --> 00:36:10,470
I'm sorry, Physics,

300
00:36:10,470 --> 00:36:12,170
for being all talk.

301
00:36:12,630 --> 00:36:14,200
Today I finally understand...

302
00:36:14,200 --> 00:36:16,430
why you wanted me to stay away from your brother.

303
00:36:17,330 --> 00:36:20,170
I'm the one who fucked up.

304
00:36:20,830 --> 00:36:23,330
But I love your brother like crazy.

305
00:36:23,330 --> 00:36:24,770
Love my brother like crazy?

306
00:36:25,870 --> 00:36:27,500
What fucking love?! / Hey, hey!

307
00:36:27,500 --> 00:36:30,670
Huh? My brother is fucking heartbroken too.

308
00:36:32,200 --> 00:36:35,970
Do you know how hard you made my brother cry?

309
00:36:38,570 --> 00:36:40,470
Chemi cried?

310
00:36:41,270 --> 00:36:44,330
But Mii was in real trouble that day. I couldn't leave her.

311
00:36:44,330 --> 00:36:46,370
How many more times do I cut you slack?

312
00:36:47,870 --> 00:36:49,870
I warned you last time.

313
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,930
What did you tell me?

314
00:36:52,930 --> 00:36:55,400
You told me this would never happen again.

315
00:36:56,230 --> 00:36:57,830
So why'd you do it again?

316
00:37:00,900 --> 00:37:02,600
This is my last warning.

317
00:37:03,600 --> 00:37:05,070
Stay away from my brother.

318
00:37:05,500 --> 00:37:06,770
Physics, but...

319
00:37:06,770 --> 00:37:08,570
Hey! Physics!

320
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:12,970
Fuen, let go of me.

321
00:37:14,170 --> 00:37:16,330
Can't you give me one more chance?

322
00:37:16,700 --> 00:37:19,400
Another chance, and then what? What will you say?

323
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:21,300
That you love my brother?

324
00:37:21,300 --> 00:37:23,800
If you really loved him, you'd have changed by now.

325
00:37:24,830 --> 00:37:29,130
Do you even realize? You say one thing and do another.

326
00:37:29,870 --> 00:37:32,200
You want me to play the fool and trust you?

327
00:37:34,170 --> 00:37:35,930
You should wise up already.

328
00:37:36,470 --> 00:37:37,870
And let my brother go.

329
00:37:37,870 --> 00:37:40,470
That's the one thing I just can't do.

330
00:37:40,770 --> 00:37:41,830
That's enough, Physics.

331
00:37:41,830 --> 00:37:44,600
You can hit me as many times as you want.

332
00:37:44,600 --> 00:37:47,170
But can't you give me a chance?

333
00:37:51,530 --> 00:37:53,300
A chance?

334
00:37:55,270 --> 00:37:57,930
A chance, after seeing my brother cry like that?

335
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:04,730
As your friend, I'm sorry,

336
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:09,900
but you're all talk.

337
00:38:13,030 --> 00:38:14,530
No chance.

338
00:38:15,930 --> 00:38:16,930
Physics!

339
00:38:17,670 --> 00:38:18,670
Physics!

340
00:38:18,670 --> 00:38:20,600
Aof, that's enough for today.

341
00:38:26,230 --> 00:38:28,130
Give him some time.

342
00:38:43,100 --> 00:38:45,530
You're always full of surprises.

343
00:38:47,230 --> 00:38:50,500
It's a shame we won't see it through together.

344
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:57,900
But I understand. It's good you know early what you want to do.

345
00:38:59,330 --> 00:39:00,500
Thank you, Coach.

346
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:03,800
I'm off to practice.

347
00:39:07,070 --> 00:39:08,170
Chemi.

348
00:39:17,230 --> 00:39:20,370
I'm sorry, Chemi, for not telling you what I was doing first.

349
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:24,000
But I really didn't mean to leave you.

350
00:39:26,600 --> 00:39:33,230
Do you know your words and your actions don't match?

351
00:39:34,330 --> 00:39:37,370
You say you didn't mean to leave me,

352
00:39:38,030 --> 00:39:39,770
but you did.

353
00:39:40,430 --> 00:39:43,700
You even know what kind of person you are,

354
00:39:45,030 --> 00:39:48,130
and you still want me to trust you.

355
00:39:49,870 --> 00:39:55,600
Did you think I'd just wait around for you like an idiot?

356
00:39:55,600 --> 00:39:58,030
That's not it, Chemi. I never thought that. But...

357
00:39:58,400 --> 00:40:00,930
My friend was in trouble. I couldn't leave my friend.

358
00:40:00,930 --> 00:40:03,030
Once I'd helped her, I rushed right to you.

359
00:40:03,030 --> 00:40:03,830
But, Chemi...

360
00:40:03,830 --> 00:40:05,130
You couldn't leave your friend.

361
00:40:06,700 --> 00:40:08,630
But you could leave me.

362
00:40:18,200 --> 00:40:20,500
I'm asking seriously.

363
00:40:22,500 --> 00:40:28,530
Did you ever care, or ever think about me at all?

364
00:40:30,930 --> 00:40:33,200
That's not it, Chemi. I think of you all the time.

365
00:40:33,200 --> 00:40:34,500
Just stop, Aof.

366
00:40:37,500 --> 00:40:39,400
I don't want to hear it anymore.

367
00:40:42,900 --> 00:40:45,330
I can't trust you anymore.

368
00:40:46,500 --> 00:40:47,970
I've had enough

369
00:40:48,500 --> 00:40:50,630
of everything about you.

370
00:40:52,270 --> 00:40:54,970
Did I say something wrong again, Chemi?

371
00:40:57,700 --> 00:41:02,900
No. You didn't say anything wrong.

372
00:41:05,330 --> 00:41:07,470
It's my fault for expecting anything.

373
00:41:09,830 --> 00:41:10,830
And from now on,

374
00:41:10,830 --> 00:41:13,030
you don't need to try anymore.

375
00:41:14,070 --> 00:41:15,230
I don't want it anymore.

376
00:41:15,230 --> 00:41:16,370
Chemi.

377
00:41:18,300 --> 00:41:19,430
Chemi!

378
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:28,500
Damn it!

379
00:41:47,130 --> 00:41:49,430
Man, why is he acting like this?

380
00:41:49,430 --> 00:41:52,170
If there were a ball right here, I'd kick it straight in his face.

381
00:41:52,900 --> 00:41:54,700
And I'd jump up and bite his ear.

382
00:41:54,700 --> 00:41:56,730
Still not satisfied, buddy?

383
00:41:56,730 --> 00:41:58,200
I'd kick his legs too.

384
00:41:58,200 --> 00:41:59,670
Enough.

385
00:42:06,130 --> 00:42:08,070
Don't go quiet on us, man.

386
00:42:08,070 --> 00:42:11,170
At least vent to me. I want to hear it.

387
00:42:17,130 --> 00:42:20,830
I'm fine with you leaving the club, but don't shut us out like this.

388
00:42:21,530 --> 00:42:23,370
I'm not okay.

389
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,500
I just need some time.

390
00:42:27,270 --> 00:42:32,170
I'll be okay. Thanks.

391
00:43:03,130 --> 00:43:08,630
Twin... Twinkle... Twinkle?

392
00:43:13,500 --> 00:43:17,230
It can't be Twinkle Little Star, can it?

393
00:43:48,100 --> 00:43:49,730
What are you doing, Din?

394
00:43:50,300 --> 00:43:51,400
Whoa!

395
00:43:55,830 --> 00:43:59,430
Guess all you want, you'll never get it.

396
00:44:00,530 --> 00:44:03,730
I just wanted to try guessing.

397
00:44:08,600 --> 00:44:11,900
You have a meeting first today, right?

398
00:44:13,530 --> 00:44:17,000
Yeah. Shouldn't take long. Why?

399
00:44:17,600 --> 00:44:18,900
No reason.

400
00:44:19,370 --> 00:44:22,630
Then come back quickly after your meeting.

401
00:44:23,430 --> 00:44:26,570
I'd like to take you out to eat.

402
00:44:32,370 --> 00:44:35,470
Sure. Dinner tonight, then.

403
00:44:52,630 --> 00:44:56,430
So how's the plan to push Din going?

404
00:44:56,970 --> 00:44:58,730
It's going great.

405
00:44:58,730 --> 00:45:02,030
But lately Din and Star seem to be doing just fine on their own.

406
00:45:02,400 --> 00:45:04,330
So I'm just going to sit back and watch.

407
00:45:05,200 --> 00:45:07,170
Why are you suddenly rooting for Din?

408
00:45:07,170 --> 00:45:09,400
Star liked Physics at first.

409
00:45:11,070 --> 00:45:14,070
Sure, my friend liked him, but as his friend,

410
00:45:14,070 --> 00:45:16,530
I have to pick what's best for him, right?

411
00:45:16,530 --> 00:45:19,500
Din, though? He ticks every box.

412
00:45:23,000 --> 00:45:26,430
Oh... What about me?

413
00:45:28,330 --> 00:45:29,870
What's my score?

414
00:45:31,170 --> 00:45:34,630
What? I already answered that day.

415
00:45:35,530 --> 00:45:38,000
Come on, that day was that day.

416
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:42,270
Today, I want to know how much of your heart I've won.

417
00:46:01,930 --> 00:46:03,870
Hey, what are you guys doing?

418
00:46:09,830 --> 00:46:11,300
Hello.

419
00:46:12,170 --> 00:46:15,370
Hey, and you...

420
00:46:15,370 --> 00:46:16,530
Oh.

421
00:46:17,300 --> 00:46:19,000
I'm shooting content for the council.

422
00:46:19,830 --> 00:46:21,230
This song's trending right now.

423
00:46:22,400 --> 00:46:24,000
Wait, where's Din?

424
00:46:24,370 --> 00:46:25,700
On his way.

425
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:28,100
He's walking Star to the car first.

426
00:46:28,400 --> 00:46:30,030
As for today's meeting,

427
00:46:30,030 --> 00:46:32,300
keep it short and to the point,

428
00:46:32,300 --> 00:46:35,130
because he's got dinner with Star after.

429
00:46:41,870 --> 00:46:46,200
"Today's mission" / "Cancel for now" / "Din's killing it!!!"

430
00:46:47,600 --> 00:46:48,700
What are you doing?

431
00:46:49,430 --> 00:46:51,630
Uh, nothing.

432
00:46:51,630 --> 00:46:54,430
Uh, shall we keep practicing the dance?

433
00:46:54,970 --> 00:46:56,370
Your turn. Come on.

434
00:46:58,300 --> 00:47:00,030
Want to join in?

435
00:47:14,570 --> 00:47:16,430
You've come to look at this a few times.

436
00:47:16,430 --> 00:47:18,700
Like it? If you do, I'll give you a discount.

437
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:23,370
What's your best price?

438
00:47:23,370 --> 00:47:24,470
38,000.

439
00:47:24,470 --> 00:47:25,600
That's rock bottom.

440
00:47:28,470 --> 00:47:29,700
Can you go any lower?

441
00:47:29,700 --> 00:47:32,730
Haggle any more and it's back to 39,000.

442
00:47:33,230 --> 00:47:35,330
Then I'll stop haggling.

443
00:47:54,670 --> 00:48:00,330
Bro, I think this one's really beautiful.

444
00:48:04,100 --> 00:48:06,100
Oh my God.

445
00:48:17,500 --> 00:48:23,070
"Chemi, I'm sorry. What do I have to do for you to stop being mad at me?"

446
00:49:08,170 --> 00:49:09,500
You possessed or something?

447
00:49:09,770 --> 00:49:10,900
No.

448
00:49:10,900 --> 00:49:13,370
But I've made up my mind. From now on,

449
00:49:13,370 --> 00:49:15,770
I'm going to be a good captain for Thapfah, our school.

450
00:49:15,770 --> 00:49:17,800
And a good example for you guys too.

451
00:49:19,070 --> 00:49:21,030
What got into you?

452
00:49:21,930 --> 00:49:23,570
All right, everyone, listen up.

453
00:49:24,570 --> 00:49:27,100
In two weeks, we've got a big tournament.

454
00:49:27,600 --> 00:49:31,800
Everyone needs to train harder and take good care of your bodies.

455
00:49:31,800 --> 00:49:34,930
Because from now on, training's going to get tougher. Understood?

456
00:49:34,930 --> 00:49:36,200
Yes, Coach!

457
00:49:36,200 --> 00:49:38,470
Aof, Thanop.

458
00:49:38,470 --> 00:49:40,800
You two have to be the backbone of this team.

459
00:49:43,400 --> 00:49:44,900
Let's give it everything we've got

460
00:49:45,400 --> 00:49:48,170
and bring the championship home to our Thapfah Wittayanusorn School.

461
00:49:48,170 --> 00:49:49,570
Let's train hard.

462
00:49:49,570 --> 00:49:51,130
Come on! / Let's go!

463
00:49:53,470 --> 00:49:58,030
Damn... That's a chemical reaction, all right.

464
00:50:07,930 --> 00:50:09,230
Excuse me.

465
00:50:09,630 --> 00:50:12,000
Can I practice one more song?

466
00:50:14,430 --> 00:50:17,930
I just don't want to be alone.

467
00:50:18,630 --> 00:50:21,230
It'll only make me sadder.

468
00:50:22,600 --> 00:50:24,000
Oh.

469
00:50:27,430 --> 00:50:34,900
Then you pick the next song, Chemi. Two songs, even. Or three.

470
00:50:35,600 --> 00:50:38,530
Four songs. We'll stay till morning.

471
00:50:38,530 --> 00:50:40,030
Until you're not sad anymore.

472
00:51:56,730 --> 00:51:59,970
The student council guys sent these for you.

473
00:52:01,300 --> 00:52:02,730
Thank you.

474
00:52:02,730 --> 00:52:05,330
But you guys should have the snacks.

475
00:52:05,900 --> 00:52:08,800
And there's something special for you too.

476
00:52:08,800 --> 00:52:10,600
For me? / Yes.

477
00:52:10,600 --> 00:52:14,770
"Warm honey lemon for the singer"

478
00:52:25,930 --> 00:52:27,570
Nice work, kid.

479
00:52:27,570 --> 00:52:29,570
I don't need compliments.

480
00:52:29,570 --> 00:52:31,730
I just want my reward.

481
00:52:38,270 --> 00:52:39,870
Thank you.

482
00:52:56,830 --> 00:53:01,530
Hmm, it's pricey. Can you handle it?

483
00:53:01,530 --> 00:53:03,070
Whatever it costs, I'm in.

484
00:53:03,070 --> 00:53:04,830
You sure you can handle it?

485
00:53:05,100 --> 00:53:06,700
Absolutely.

486
00:53:10,630 --> 00:53:12,570
5,500. / Huh?

487
00:53:13,030 --> 00:53:15,070
I thought you said you could handle it.

488
00:53:18,370 --> 00:53:20,670
Got the guts or not?

489
00:53:22,100 --> 00:53:24,570
Bag this one up for me.

490
00:53:25,570 --> 00:53:27,430
You got it, kid.

491
00:53:30,430 --> 00:53:32,130
I'll scan to pay.

492
00:55:03,400 --> 00:55:05,030
Isn't this a bit much, man?

493
00:55:06,270 --> 00:55:07,900
Nah, man.

494
00:55:08,430 --> 00:55:10,030
I picked all of it out for you.

495
00:55:10,030 --> 00:55:13,270
Once you get all this, you're set.

496
00:55:14,000 --> 00:55:15,570
Wait...

497
00:55:18,900 --> 00:55:21,230
Start with these basics first.

498
00:55:22,230 --> 00:55:24,700
I know you're not great with tenses.

499
00:55:25,000 --> 00:55:27,470
Vocab you can memorize later.

500
00:55:35,430 --> 00:55:36,800
Ready?

501
00:55:39,200 --> 00:55:40,300
Ready, I guess.

502
00:55:42,300 --> 00:55:44,330
Hey, come here.

503
00:55:44,870 --> 00:55:46,030
What?

504
00:55:46,570 --> 00:55:48,000
Turn around, turn around.

505
00:55:56,030 --> 00:55:57,230
What's this?

506
00:55:59,200 --> 00:56:00,170
Good?

507
00:56:00,170 --> 00:56:01,470
Here, let me fix your hair.

508
00:56:02,070 --> 00:56:03,100
Ready.

509
00:56:03,670 --> 00:56:04,870
Get set.

510
00:56:10,170 --> 00:56:11,230
Let's go!

511
00:56:13,030 --> 00:56:14,100
Yeah, start from here.

512
00:56:14,100 --> 00:56:14,800
Okay.

513
00:56:16,870 --> 00:56:20,130
Look, there's Thai here for you to read. Understand it first.

514
00:56:20,130 --> 00:56:23,600
Don't rush into the English. That's too advanced.

515
00:56:24,600 --> 00:56:30,130
♪ Looking at the photos some nights before I sleep, I smile to myself ♪

516
00:56:30,130 --> 00:56:34,330
♪ Every time I think back on those nights, on you and me ♪

517
00:56:34,330 --> 00:56:39,530
♪ a time I've never once forgotten ♪

518
00:56:42,200 --> 00:56:50,600
♪ However long the years run on, my heart still won't forget ♪

519
00:56:50,600 --> 00:56:58,000
♪ Even if we had to part in the end, that time is still just as it was ♪

520
00:56:58,000 --> 00:57:02,000
♪ It's all still so clear inside me ♪

521
00:57:02,000 --> 00:57:06,200
♪ I still remember all our good times, just the same ♪

522
00:57:06,200 --> 00:57:10,470
♪ The days we smiled at each other, the days we were close ♪

523
00:57:10,500 --> 00:57:15,200
♪ None of it has ever gone away ♪

524
00:57:16,200 --> 00:57:17,700
What are you doing?

525
00:57:19,800 --> 00:57:21,130
Nothing.

526
00:57:23,330 --> 00:57:25,170
Why'd you stop reading?

527
00:57:26,170 --> 00:57:27,930
Ask first before you do anything.

528
00:57:27,930 --> 00:57:29,570
But I'll let that one slide.

529
00:57:29,570 --> 00:57:31,170
Let's say I was asleep.

530
00:57:35,830 --> 00:57:38,470
You're not focusing.

531
00:57:49,530 --> 00:57:51,430
Oh, hello. / Hello.

532
00:57:52,130 --> 00:57:54,700
Oh, bye-bye.

533
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:02,400
"I gave it to you, Star. Why'd you give it to your friends?"

534
00:58:04,070 --> 00:58:05,500
Bye, Star. Thanks for the snacks.

535
00:58:05,500 --> 00:58:07,000
Enjoy.

536
00:58:07,530 --> 00:58:08,730
Hey!

537
00:58:27,070 --> 00:58:29,170
"Thanks for staying by me. I'm scared as hell."

538
00:58:29,170 --> 00:58:31,330
"How'd I cope without you? Thanks, Physics." (Fuen)

539
00:58:31,330 --> 00:58:34,330
"I'll try to tell Dad the truth. It must've been hard on you, Aof."

540
00:58:34,330 --> 00:58:36,330
"I'm sorry. I'm really, truly sorry." (Memii)

541
00:58:36,870 --> 00:58:40,700
"I just wanted to pick you up so we could go to school together." (Din)

542
00:58:41,400 --> 00:58:43,470
He's shown me a bunch of universities.

543
00:58:43,470 --> 00:58:46,430
So what do you think, Fuen? Study together, or somewhere else?

544
00:58:46,430 --> 00:58:48,070
You can stop trying to guess.

545
00:58:48,070 --> 00:58:49,430
Is it that obvious on my face?

546
00:58:49,430 --> 00:58:52,070
He's studying hard, so no whining, got it?

547
00:58:52,070 --> 00:58:53,100
Dad!

548
00:58:53,100 --> 00:58:55,770
I've got a big match this Sunday. Will you come watch me, Chemi?

549
00:58:55,770 --> 00:58:56,630
I'm busy.

550
00:58:56,630 --> 00:58:58,930
But can I have one more chance?

551
00:59:00,130 --> 00:59:01,930
Up to you.

552
00:59:03,030 --> 00:59:04,030
Thanop.

553
00:59:04,030 --> 00:59:05,600
I need five goals on my own today.

554
00:59:05,600 --> 00:59:08,130
Dreaming? / I don't have any other choice.

555
00:59:08,130 --> 00:59:10,270
Football's the only thing I'm good at.

556
00:59:10,270 --> 00:59:12,470
Aof, I can't do that.

557
00:59:12,470 --> 00:59:14,100
Or you'll be their target all game.

558
00:59:14,100 --> 00:59:15,230
He's rarely this fired up.

559
00:59:15,230 --> 00:59:16,600
Coach, why not give him a shot?

560
00:59:16,600 --> 00:59:19,330
Three, two, one... Thapfah!
